<title>FRANCE: NYK top destination for Feb Paris cargo exports.</title>
<headline>NYK top destination for Feb Paris cargo exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in February 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports in February 1997</p>
<p>and the percentage change on February 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    Destination     Feb '97   pct change</p>
<p> 1  New York	  2,877   up    4.5pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   2,324   up   21.1</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo	     2,055   down 17.7</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	 1,667   up   15.2</p>
<p> 5  Sao Paulo	 1,242   up   75.3</p>
<p> 6  Mexico City     1,218   up   32.5</p>
<p> 7  Montreal	  1,196   down  3.2</p>
<p> 8  Los Angeles	 952   down  1.1</p>
<p> 9  Singapore	   847   up   50.1</p>
<p> 10 Miami		 638   up   36.9</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
